 },
 "reading": "Two things the pseudo-code of clause 6.2.2.4 does not print: the coupling channel has the low-frequency compensation while its bands are below 22, and the last band of a channel looks at no band after it. Read as the clause prints it, 870 of the 2 879 frames of four streams end in a mantissa code that does not exist, a group above its range or past the end of the frame, and the Dolby decode has ordinary audio in every one of them; with the first rule alone 659 are lost, with the second alone 323, with both none. Below 1,2 kHz, where each channel codes its own bins, a median frame of the two streams without a transient is then within 88.8 to 89.3 dB of the Dolby decode, the channel that carries a sweep within 68.1 dB. Nothing else moves: of 129 streams the four change and 125 do not, over 8 756 lines and 55 120 fields of reports and 103 436 751 233 bytes of deliveries."
